'' -appkey's PASSWORDS COME FROM THE ENVIRONMENT ONLY (docs/tiko-android A6): apksigner and jarsigner
'' read TIKO_ANDROID_KS_PASS themselves, so no password is ever on a command line. Unset, the build
'' is refused before anything compiles. (The keystore only has to exist for this check.)
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_ANDROID_KS_PASS=
'' ARGS: -app -target android-x86_64 -appkey tests/source/plain.bas,release tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0197: '-appkey tests/source/plain.bas,release': set TIKO_ANDROID_KS_PASS to the keystore's password (and TIKO_ANDROID_KEY_PASS to the key's, when it differs)
